      "height": 918,
      "heading": "Know what to charge. Hold the line when they push back.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF7E8",
      "callsToAction": [
        "Try the Pricing Advisor",
        "Draft a counter-offer"
      ],
      "text": "Know what to charge. Hold the line when they push back. Freelancers and small businesses lose money twice: once by under-pricing, and again by folding the moment a client says “can you do it for less?” Parley helps with both. Try the Pricing Advisor Draft a counter-offer",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 918,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1102,
      "heading": "You're leaving money on the table twice",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF7E7",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "THE PROBLEM & THE FIX You're leaving money on the table twice Underpricing by default Most freelancers guess at rates based on what feels safe, not what the market bears or what the work is worth. 47% undercharge by 30%+ Folding under pressure When a client pushes back, the instinct is to discount immediately — losing margin and signaling low confidence. 68% discount on first pushback No repeatable process Every new project starts from zero. No framework for pricing, no template for negotiation, no institutional memory. Zero reusable assets Pricing Advisor Describe your service and client. Get",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#how-it-works",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2020,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1029,
      "heading": "From first number to a signed agreement, without the guesswork.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FBF7E8",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "From first number to a signed agreement, without the guesswork. 01 Describe the work Add the service, client, timeline, and constraints that shape the value of the engagement. Clear next step 02 Set three strong price points See a defensible floor, target, and stretch price with the rationale behind each one. Clear next step 03 Bring the pushback Paste the message when a client asks for a discount or changes the terms. Clear next step 04 Reply with leverage Get a deal-health read and a clear response that protects scope, price, and tone. Clear next step 05 Build your playbook Your previous dec",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#features",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3049,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1319,
      "heading": "Everything you need to price confidently and negotiate professionally",
      "backgroundColor": "#F8F5E8",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "WHAT YOU GET Everything you need to price confidently and negotiate professionally Pricing Advisor Tiered pricing with reasoning Three price points — floor, target, stretch — each with cost basis, market data, and value anchors explained in plain English. Negotiation Ready-to-send counter messages Professional, firm, not arrogant. Tone-matched to your style. Copy button built in. No wordsmithing required. Negotiation Deal Health Score (0-100) Instant read on whether to walk away, counter, or hold firm. Color-coded zones with clear thresholds. Platform Smart model routing Simple scopes → fast/c",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "section",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4367,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 759,
      "heading": "A sharper way to have the conversations that set your business up.",
      "backgroundColor": "#FFFFFF",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "A sharper way to have the conversations that set your business up. A price you can explain Move from a single nervous number to a clear range, with the logic that supports it. Language that keeps the relationship intact Turn an awkward reply into a practical next step without performing confidence you do not feel. A private record of your decisions Keep the context, reasoning, and outcomes from past conversations close when the next opportunity arrives.",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
